# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Ablation caches ARE TRACKED as of 2026-09-05. They were ignored as
# "regenerable, and large" — the first is true and the second was not: all
# EIGHT together are 296 KB. Tracking them lets a clone reproduce or extend the
# tables without the run. The cost is that a stale cache can now arrive with a
# checkout, so ABLATION_CACHES.md records a source fingerprint per deck; check
# it before resuming one. See cache_manifest.py.
#
# Eight, not four, since 2026-09-06: each deck has the current N=15000 cache and
# the superseded N=6000 (tivit: N=2000) one, which is kept because it is the
# provenance for every number quoted in CLAUDE.md above that date. The
# "roughly six hours to rebuild" that justified tracking them is no longer true
# either — the whole set is 23 minutes now. They stay tracked for provenance
# rather than for the compute.

# Spreadsheet lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Ablation stderr progress logs — noise, the .txt tables are the artefact
ablation_*.log

# Regeneration scratch — the finished .txt tables ARE tracked
ablation_*.txt.new
regen.log

# A void table kept only long enough to diff against; not an artefact.
ablation_*_VOID_*.txt
